  "title": "FDA Approves New Tylenol with Naproxen for OTC Pain Relief",
  "summary": "The U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) has approved a groundbreaking over-the-counter pain relief medication that combines two well-known ingredients into a single product. The newly approved Tylenol with Naproxen brings together 650 mg of acetaminophen and 220 mg of naproxen sodium, offering consumers a convenient non-prescription option for managing temporary pain. This approval marks an important milestone because it is the first FDA-approved over-the-counter fixed-dose combination of a",
